      }
    ],
    "hints": ["'git reflog' shows all recent HEAD movements", "Find the SHA of the lost commit, then 'git reset --hard <sha>'"],
    "afterSolve": "Reflog is your safety net. Git rarely truly deletes data — reflog keeps a record of where HEAD has been for about 90 days."
